{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.DqSquared","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.DqSquared","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Units","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Units.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dq_cochain_on_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dq_cochain_on_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L116-L120","doc":"On horizontal ℒ_ξ-invariant forms, dq defines a cochain complex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dq_squared_zero_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dq_squared_zero_classical","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L109-L114","doc":"dq² vanishes at q = 1 (classical limit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dq_squared_zero_reeb_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dq_squared_zero_reeb_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L102-L107","doc":"dq² vanishes on Reeb-invariant forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.dq_squared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.dq_squared","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L72-L100","doc":"**Non-vanishing of dq²** (archimedean statement of `prop:dq-squared`).\n\nFor a nondegenerate Levi form (`dθ ≠ 0`), `dq²(α) = 0 ⟺ q = 1 ∨ ℒ_ξ α = 0`:\nthe q-deformed de Rham operator fails to be a cochain differential away\nfrom the classical limit `q = 1`, except on Reeb-invariant forms. This\nis the decl named by the content block's `lean.ref`.\n\n`[IsDomain R]` is essential, not cosmetic — see the module docstring for\nthe `ℤ/6` counterexample without it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:dq-squared","label":"prop:dq-squared","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.dqSquared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.dqSquared","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L65-L70","doc":"The archimedean dq² value: `dq²(α) = q⁻¹(1 - q⁻¹) · dθ · ℒ_ξ α`.\nDefined as a function of the data so the vanishing theorem is\nnon-vacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.levi_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.levi_form","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L61-L61","doc":"The Levi form value dθ(·, ·) (scalar representative). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.lie_deriv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.lie_deriv","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The Lie derivative value ℒ_ξ α (scalar representative). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.q","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The substrate parameter q, carried as a unit (algebraic\ninvertibility — not the archimedean `0 < q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared.mk","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ArchimedeanDqSquared","kind":"structure","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/dq-squared.lean#L50-L61","doc":"**Archimedean dq² data**: substrate `q` (as a unit — the invertibility\nwitness is the unit structure itself), the Lie-derivative value `ℒ_ξ α`,\nand the Levi form `dθ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}